# Crime BRIEFLY appeared to clear the floor on 30 Jul once the lag-by-calendar-year fix was applied
# (r2 0.19->0.56), then dropped back out once its own gaps (2021-22 COVID pause, several pre-2002
# sparse-survey years) were properly interpolated rather than left as an accidentally-favourable
# truncated sample (r2 0.56->0.23 on the fuller, more honest data) — see FIG211_NOTES.md for the
# full story; not a flip-flopping bug, a genuine correction each time.
#
# UNIT FIX (30 Jul, PJ: "what is the unit these lines are calculated on... need to be the same for
# all measures"). Caught a real inconsistency: this panel was plotting each item's RAW residual in
# percentage points, never standardised — while panel B (composite) and panel C (PCA) are BOTH
# already in z-score/standardised units. Residual SD varies ~10x across items (Drugs 1.42 to Economy
# general 14.87, all_items_tracking_stats.csv), so the raw-pp version made some domains' lines look
